From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shikosu <teovidal01@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 19:47:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Linux host: a clean shutdown on SIGINT and SIGTERM, a soak
 log and a stall report (#22)

The run ended with os._exit(0) after a timer and a signal killed it with no
report. Now the end of the run, SIGINT and SIGTERM run the same ordered steps
(drain the GPU queue, report, close the mixer, last soak line), each with a time
limit, and leave with 0 or 128 plus the signal. The signal reaches a thread of
its own through a wake up descriptor, because the main thread is inside game
code most of the time. A second signal leaves at once.

NX2LINUX_SOAK_LOG=FILE writes the resident memory, threads, open files, frames
and the rate every 10 s. NX2LINUX_STALL_SECONDS=N reports once, with where the
guest threads are, when no frame was presented for N s after the first one. Both
are off unless set. tools/soak_summary.py reads the file.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream-Status: fork-only
Reason: A run stops with a report on SIGINT and SIGTERM, and a long run leaves a log of its memory, threads and frames
Issue: Sunshine-Off/NX2Linux#22

